ATTRIBUTION
-----------

Stable Diffusion on the Qualcomm Hexagon NPU
    xororz/local-dream
    https://github.com/xororz/local-dream
    Licensed CC BY-NC 4.0

    The C++ inference server in this project is a fork of local-dream's.
    The QNN pipelines, the model conversion process, the per chipset build
    tiers and the device capability gating are all that project's work.
    The Stable Diffusion checkpoint archives and the upscaler weights this
    app downloads are published by the same author.

    Modifications made here: the pipeline was decomposed into individually
    addressable ops (encode_text, sample, vae_encode, vae_decode,
    latent_blend) exposed over HTTP, with conditionings and latents held
    server side behind handles.

LocalDream
    https://github.com/AbrahamPaulJ/dreamui
    A consumer application built on the same backend.

    The mask editor's brush behaviour, its compositing rules, and the batch
    result strip are ported from it rather than reimplemented.


THIRD PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------

Qualcomm AI Runtime (QAIRT / QNN)
    Qualcomm Technologies, Inc.
    Runtime libraries used to execute models on the Hexagon NPU. Distributed
    under Qualcomm's own licence terms, which are separate from and not
    superseded by this project's licence. Not included in this repository.

QuickJS
    Fabrice Bellard and Charlie Gordon
    https://bellard.org/quickjs/
    MIT licensed. Used as the sandbox for plugin nodes. Fetched at build
    time rather than vendored.

MNN
    Alibaba
    https://github.com/alibaba/MNN
    Apache 2.0. Used for CPU and GPU model execution paths.

Real-ESRGAN x4plus anime 6B, 4x UltraSharpV2 Lite
    Upscaler weights, converted and published by xororz.
    Downloaded by the app at the user's request; not included here.


